    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8237",
      "problem": "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158151/assets/6815c74aeca5bc8e672a6ccaf3e4ff770f9c5a2cf404c574b3ae4908057e4b67.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X \\leq m) = \\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nP(X \\leq m) = F(m) = 1-\\dfrac{1}{m^4} , \\quad m \\geq 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n1-\\dfrac{1}{m^4} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad m = \\sqrt[4]2.\n$$\n\nNote that we took the positive root because $m \\geq 1.$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158151/observations/step-e8237-aa934a6565cad7c1260e.html",
